title: Clamp
golf: 35

Write `clamp(n, low, high)` that keeps n between low and high.
`clamp(15, 0, 10)` gives `10`, `clamp(-3, 0, 10)` gives `0`, and `clamp(5, 0, 10)` gives `5`.
=== starter
def clamp(n, low, high):
    ...
=== broken
def clamp(n, low, high):
    return min(low, max(n, high))
=== test
from harness import eq


def test_clamp(sol):
    eq(sol.clamp(15, 0, 10), 10, "clamp(15, 0, 10)")
    eq(sol.clamp(-3, 0, 10), 0, "clamp(-3, 0, 10)")
    eq(sol.clamp(5, 0, 10), 5, "clamp(5, 0, 10)")
